  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Montenegrin Employers Federation (MEF) is the main voice of business in Montenegro and plays a key role in informing policy and law making. However, the evolving nature of business representation - driven by regional and global trends and Montenegro&#x2019;s commitments under the EU accession process - has added complexity to the MEF&#x2019;s mandate. As a result, the MEF is in need of enhanced expertise and capacity in a growing number of policy areas. 

In 2023, the ILO supported the MEF in conducting a comprehensive Enabling Environment for Sustainable Enterprises (EESE) assessment to evaluate the evolution of the Montenegrin business environment and identify future reform priorities. The assessment commended improvements in certain areas while noting that progress is still lagging in others. Additional reforms are key to help Montenegrin enterprises navigate the evolving business landscape, build resilience, and ensure their long-term competitiveness. These reforms are also crucial to the process of EU accession. 

Activities for 2024-2025 are strategically designed to enhance the MEF&#x2019;s advocacy capabilities and strengthen its role as a policy actor. The proposed approach focuses on developing and launching a new business agenda drawing on the EESE assessment. Additional support will be provided to build the MEF&#x2019;s capacity to develop an advocacy and communication plan to guide its interactions with policymakers and other stakeholders in a more systematic and impactful manner. 

Follow-up research will be conducted in areas stemming from the new business agenda that need further analysis. These include productivity, responsible business conduct, and the just transition, with the latter to focus on the impact of Nationally Determined Contributions (NDCs) on the private sector. Finally, the ILO will facilitate a policy forum to strengthen the MEF&#x2019;s capacity to advocate for incentive-based strategies to tackle informality.</narrative>
  </description>
